 Skills entirely and the like. CofD seems to avoid doing that sort of thing, and it'd probably be good for compatibility anyway.<br /> <br /> That's guesswork on my part though. I'm excited to see the result, regardless!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T18:16:41-07:00","id":1131540,"title":"","content":"Aw yiss. Never player Innocents, but enjoyed reading it a lot. Nothing is scarier than a little girl in a horror movie.<br /> <br /> Also seconding the idea for monster kids. Give me Claudia and Eli! A story with Mike, Dustin and Lucas, the little Beast Richard from the Conquering Heroes prologue, Teenage Werewolves, Davina and Monique like witches...<br /> I can totally dig this =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T21:11:51-07:00","id":1131601,"title":"","content":"So I'm curious; how will this differ from the 1e book? I'm sure it won't just be a retread, and you can only spend so much room ranting about how good Stranger Things was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T06:58:06-07:00","id":1131689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1131601#post1131601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm curious; how will this differ from the 1e book? I'm sure it won't just be a retread, and you can only spend so much room ranting about how good Stranger Things was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wormwood and I have our theory. More monster child support seems like it would be an easy thing to add to the book. Maybe a guide to making our own supernatural school setting in the book as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1131540#post1131540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aw yiss. Never player Innocents, but enjoyed reading it a lot. Nothing is scarier than a little girl in a horror movie.<br /> <br /> Also seconding the idea for monster kids. Give me Claudia and Eli! A story with Mike, Dustin and Lucas, the little Beast Richard from the Conquering Heroes prologue, Teenage Werewolves, Davina and Monique like witches...<br /> I can totally dig this =D</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter in Darkness Ame and Iron Master Yuki!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:35:35-07:00","id":1131804,"title":"","content":"I wonder if they're planning to make a book for adults about playing children of Chronicles of Darkness, or if they're designing this with the intent that it be marketed to children (kind of like pugmire sort of is aimed to both kids and adults.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:43:38-07:00","id":1131809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1131804#post1131804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if they're planning to make a book for adults about playing children of Chronicles of Darkness, or if they're designing this with the intent that it be marketed to children (kind of like pugmire sort of is aimed to both kids and adults.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It will most assuredly be the former. CofD is explicitly for an adult audience and Innocents 1e was about playing children in nWoD, not about targeting a demographic that the game isn't meant for. It could be interesting to have a section of the Storyteller's section be about introducing the games to younger players, but it would have to be handled extremely carefully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:49:22-07:00","id":1131811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1131809#post1131809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It will most assuredly be the former. CofD is explicitly for an adult audience and Innocents 1e was about playing children in nWoD, not about targeting a demographic that the game isn't meant for. It could be interesting to have a section of the Storyteller's section be about introducing the games to younger players, but it would have to be handled extremely carefully.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas. I think it could be neat to have a CofD gameline aimed at kids while staying canon with the main games. Would make it easier to run games for nieces and nephews. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:59:01-07:00","id":1131816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1131811#post1131811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alas. I think it could be neat to have a CofD gameline aimed at kids while staying canon with the main games. Would make it easier to run games for nieces and nephews. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I agree. I am fully intent on playing RPGs with my and my sister's kids (not that they exist yet). In fact, one of my motivations for picking Mage to add to 1001 Nights for DE2 is so that Mage's canon has a version of my partner's religion that doesn't paint them as hedonists and heretics (the current canon was written in early days with a different understanding of the importance of cultural representation). That way I can pull double duty of playing an RPG and teaching my kids some family history.<br /> <br /> I think that's something that has to be done at the individual level. All of CofD's books to date carry a &quot;mature content&quot; label, so having to distinguish between the books that would be kid-friendly and those that aren't would be too much of a headache for OPP and for parents/guardians. Not worth it. Plus, that would be huge departure from Innocents 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T15:52:03-07:00","id":1131924,"title":"","content":"The Monster Kids were less a theory and more a &quot;omg yes please&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T18:33:29-07:00","id":1131981,"title":"","content":"Wasn't Innocents 1e using a different standard of stats than the adult gamelines? I wouldn't mind it being more crossoverable. My group includes the younger teen titans as well as adults, I wouldn't mind this book to fit into the greater mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:07:27-07:00","id":1132045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1131981#post1131981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't Innocents 1e using a different standard of stats than the adult gamelines? I wouldn't mind it being more crossoverable. My group includes the younger teen titans as well as adults, I wouldn't mind this book to fit into the greater mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I want Innocents 2E to end with 'kids use different stats', as I'm really low on running kids only game. Best, from my perspective, would be to add kids special Conditions chain that limit's their normal stats, especially as fact is that in school we learn MANY things we later not use in life, that 'moves' to different skills in adult life. And as those are Conditions, they let get nice Beats for child character, more than adult character, but still using normal rules in mixing groups. Win-Win. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For seeing what exactly I have in mind, just see our <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/982910-2e-innocents-children-in-cod?p=1005718#post1005718\">Innocents Fan 2E Update topic</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/982910-2e-innocents-children-in-cod?p=1005718#post1005718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Returning to topic with my straight forward compilation of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> ideas. I added only Attributes cap on <i>Child</i> Condition, but still think that maybe using general -1 penalty to all actions based on Attributes past 3, maybe?<br /> <br /> General idea is that young child ( 7-12ish ) would begin with <i>Child</i>, while a young adult (17-20ish) would start with <i>Adolescent</i>. A Teenager (13-16ish) would get the worst of both worlds and start with both Conditions.<br /> <br /> <b>Child (Persistent)</b><br /> Your character is a pre-adolescent (typically between 7-12 years of age). Character at this stage of development have several disadvantages when compared to an adult; their base size is 4, their Speed factor is 4, and any unarmed attack made against an adult or adult sized creature suffers a -2 penalty. You cannot raise any of her Attributes and Skills above 3 dots. Additionally, you do not benefit from the 10-again quality on teamwork actions that involve adult characters, and adult characters gain the 8-again quality on Contested actions against her. However, the characters smaller stature works to their advantage in some situations; against adults they gain a +1 die bonus to Stealth, Breaking Free of Grapple, or when Dodging.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> When your character reaches physical maturity.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> When the characters youth causes a significant social or physical set back (especially when dealing with adults).<br /> <br /> <b>Adolescent (Persistent)</b><br /> Your character is in an awkward transitionary phase of development - no longer a child, but not yet an adult, she struggles to find her place in the world. Adults tend to assume the worst in your character until she proves her maturity to them. You begin all Social Maneuvering attempts with adult characters at a Hostile impression.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> You face prejudice or discrimination as a result of your age.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Your character reaches developmental maturity.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:16:50-07:00","id":1132049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1132045#post1132045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I want Innocents 2E to end with 'kids use different stats', as I'm really low on running kids only game. Best, from my perspective, would be to add kids special Conditions chain that limit's their normal stats, especially as fact is that in school we learn MANY things we later not use in life, that 'moves' to different skills in adult life. And as those are Conditions, they let get nice Beats for child character, more than adult character, but still using normal rules in mixing groups. Win-Win. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For seeing what exactly I have in mind, just see our <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/982910-2e-innocents-children-in-cod?p=1005718#post1005718&amp;quot;]Innocents</a> Fan 2E Update topic[/URL].<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While the idea of conditions to represent childhood has potential, both of those would actively make me not want to play young characters. And as a high school teacher, I find it really fucking offensive that the adolescent condition makes all adults hostile. That's flat out BS, we work our asses off for our kids and try to give them the benefit of the doubt unless we have a good reason not to. This points to my primary concern about conditions in Innocent 2e: it becomes really easy to generalize. The experience of a 14 year old in Canada is completely different from in India or in Congo. The modern teenage experience is entirely different from the 18th century, the 9th century, the rise of civilizations, or from the Neolithic. CofD now covers all of those eras and each has compelling reasons to play younger characters in them. <br /> <br /> Whoever writes Innocents has their work cut out for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:27:08-07:00","id":1132055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1132049#post1132049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the idea of conditions to represent childhood has potential, both of those would actively make me not want to play young characters. And as a high school teacher, I find it really fucking offensive that the adolescent condition makes all adults hostile. That's flat out BS, we work our asses off for our kids and try to give them the benefit of the doubt unless we have a good reason not to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not saying they were really good - it was quickly made mix od Charl's, Reinghalls and a bit of mine ideas, not really tested. So it was just propostion that would need to be hammered by at least 3 revisions and hard playtests. I easily can see this 'Hostile in Social Manuvering' to be one of things that need to dissapear from it in final take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1132049#post1132049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This points to my primary concern about conditions in Innocent 2e: it becomes really easy to generalize. The experience of a 14 year old in Canada is completely different from in India or in Congo. The modern teenage experience is entirely different from the 18th century, the 9th century, the rise of civilizations, or from the Neolithic. CofD now covers all of those eras and each has compelling reasons to play younger characters in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you look like this, than <b><i>any</i></b> Character Creation rules in CoD should be rewritten - 'We cannot have that adult's humans have 22 dots - in America we have higher education, so we should starts with free Computers and Academics. And in India we do not have those as risen, so you need to put <i>extra</i> dot into Academics to have the same level as Americans.' ( It's something made up, just on pseudo-reasons. ) And historical takes also applies to adults - before circa 1850, most of population in any country was illiterate.<br /> <br /> <b>It's RPG, not real life</b> - some liberites need to be taken just to have some common ground in rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-21-2017, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:37:47-07:00","id":1132060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1132055#post1132055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not saying they were really good - it was quickly made mix od Charl's, Reinghalls and a bit of mine ideas, not really tested. So it was just propostion that would need to be hammered by at least 3 revisions and hard playtests. I easily can see this 'Hostile in Social Manuvering' to be one of things that need to dissapear from it in final take.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you look like this, than <b><i>any</i></b> Character Creation rules in CoD should be rewritten - 'We cannot have that adult's humans have 22 dots - in America we have higher education, so we should starts with free Computers and Academics. And in India we do not have those as risen, so you need to put <i>extra</i> dot into Academics to have the same level as Americans.' ( It's something made up, just on pseudo-reasons. ) And historical takes also applies to adults - before circa 1850, most of population in any country was illiterate.<br /> <br /> <b>It's RPG, not real life</b> - some liberites need to be taken just to have some common ground in rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a big difference between taking liberaties for the sake of a game and assuming the &quot;default&quot; of humanity is a western, modern perspective. It is entirely fair for me wanting to see Innocents presented as a baseline from which you can build any culture or time period equally. There a many biases to be aware of in childhood be they cultural, socio-economic, historical, racial, or ablistic. All of them need to be navigated carefully. Innocents 1e did a good job of that, so my hopes are high. <br /> <br /> And I think that North Americans gettting extra Academics and Computers over Indians would be exactly the type of thing I don't want to see, so I feel like my point is being missed here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T15:14:19-07:00","id":1132407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1132060#post1132060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a big difference between taking liberaties for the sake of a game and assuming the &quot;default&quot; of humanity is a western, modern perspective. It is entirely fair for me wanting to see Innocents presented as a baseline from which you can build any culture or time period equally. There a many biases to be aware of in childhood be they cultural, socio-economic, historical, racial, or ablistic. All of them need to be navigated carefully. Innocents 1e did a good job of that, so my hopes are high.<br /> <br /> And I think that North Americans gettting extra Academics and Computers over Indians would be exactly the type of thing I don't want to see, so I feel like my point is being missed here.</div> </div> </div> </div>A overview of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_childhood\" target=\"_blank\">history of childhood</a> would be the best way to do that for space reasons, in my opinion. the Modern western youth lifestyle doesn't really exist until the 50s and the idea of children as something other than mini adults doesn't exist until the 1600s<br /> <br /> J<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T03:37:29-07:00","id":1132554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1131689#post1131689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More monster child support seems like it would be an easy thing to add to the book. </div> </div> </div> </div>Yes please.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1131689#post1131689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe a guide to making our own supernatural school setting in the book as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please no. If we're talking anime-style school of monster kids, it doesn't fit the setting at all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T06:20:09-07:00","id":1132578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1132554#post1132554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please no. If we're talking anime-style school of monster kids, it doesn't fit the setting at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, to an extent, even though a &quot;Hogwarts for tiny Mages&quot; would be fun - and utterly terrifying. The moment you put a bunch of puberty-stricken children full of magic into one room, you have the same problems as a normal school with access to things children/adolescents should not have access to for reasons. (This obviously comes down to the individuals - there are classes I wouldn't mind bending the rules a little to let them have a more interesting experiment, and there are classes I am hesitant to let them do the most simple experiments on their own, because of lack of discipline and ability.) I mean, just think back to your time in school. Now imagine you had Mind 2, Space 2, Forces 1 (or any other combination of Arcana, just throwing something out here). Imagine how that might've changed your behaviour. And now, imagine everyone had something like that.<br /> So yeah, something like a &quot;Boku no Hero Academia&quot; type school would work for me, refluffed correctly to fit the setting. A Mage-only school for Sleepwalkers and Awakened, whose Mentors want to prepare early for the life ahead of them. Strip down the &quot;Superhero/Fighting&quot; theme, increase the &quot;prodigious and exclusive education&quot; one, and you end up with a &quot;Magic Nerd&quot; school that let's young Mages explore the Worlds in a more-or-less controlled setting, hone their abilities to become the next generation of highly successful Arrows/Guardians/etc. Subjects include &quot;Spirit Lore&quot;, &quot;Medicine&quot;, &quot;Physics&quot;, &quot;Phys Ed&quot; and &quot;Handling unknown magical objects&quot;. Physics would of course not just be Fallen Physics, Medicine would feature Life heavily, and Phys Ed would feature things like running fast, running for a long time, and free running much more prominently rather than Basketball or Football. Size would be more that of a small town school, not that of a school serving for all people in a huge area which seems so much more common in the U.S. It would probably start seemingly harmless, then quickly turn dark. This is still a Horror game, and they ARE messing with Supernal Powers, after all. Can totally see a Spirit-Lesson on the Uratha go wrong when they thoughtlessly and accidentally desecrate the territory of e.g. a pack of Hunters in Darkness, or problems occuring when a simple spell in Medicine goes horribly wrong and the caster botches the Paradox roll. A young Mastigos overestimates his skills and messes with the wrong Vampire, the Seers take note of the Pentacle school and guide in some Hunters, and just WHAT the hell is in the basement that the Headmaster forbids entering it on threats of expulsion and worse? For that matter, what if the Headmaster or another Teacher is actually a Left-handed path member leading the kids down another road? What if this LOOKS like a school, but actually isn't? It is preparing the grounds for a Scelestus big ceremonial summoning of an abyssal creature - the sacrifice for the Spell? The unwitting and betrayed students. Or this is a lifestock experiment for a Lich, teaching children how to defend, but carefully leaving out certain things to have an opening when they challenge him. And challenge him they will, once &quot;expulsed&quot; kids never reach home, and they start getting suspicious...<br /> aaaaanyway, that'd be my take on it.<br /> <br /> A school where a freshly-changed Ghost Wolf stumbles upon the eternally-16 year old Ghoul of a Vampire, where an Aurum Promethean is currently trying to fit in? Maybe throw in a Beast teacher for good measure? Sounds like a fun premise for a game.<br /> <br /> After all, it's about what you make of it.<br /> I can see why you'd be hesitant about an anime-style school of monster kids, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T06:51:10-07:00","id":1132590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way#post1131071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As per GenCon, the Second Edition of Innocents is now in play! Super excited for this one. A big reason for its success was that the writers worked with kids, were professionals in the field, and held degrees relating to child development. I hope they go that route again and it sounds like they are.<br /> <br /> Discuss and rejoice!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is the BEST! The enjoyable game I ever ran was an Innocent Geist: Sin Eaters game, or as my group called it &quot;playing dead little kids&quot; game set in a fictional town in Alaska we made with a collaborative setting creating game. Can't wait until they've updated the rules for 2ed and I can use them because my ad hoc Childhood as a set of Conditions which affect Mental, Social and Physical aspects of a character works but is a bit cumbersome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T10:59:08-07:00","id":1132702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1132554#post1132554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please no. If we're talking anime-style school of monster kids, it doesn't fit the setting at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not some kind of Scooby Doo's Ghoul School, but as Wormwood said some kind of Mage school could be fun, and other groups have their own possibilities. Heirs to Hell distinctly brings up the concept of a Demon Blooded Academy. Some kind of pseudo Military School that helps train their youngsters to take care of themselves. Perhaps even going as far as training on various Embeds within the confines of the schoolwork. Even Occult classes framed as World Religion if they ever need to handle outside intrusion from Mortal agencies looking in on the school as a school.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T12:20:55-07:00","id":1132745,"title":"","content":"And for Vampire, there could be rhe write-up of the Children's Crusade covenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T19:59:54-07:00","id":1132891,"title":"","content":"I think that would veer into <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Black_Dog\" target=\"_blank\">Black Dog</a> ter