6 year old Ghoul of a Vampire, where an Aurum Promethean is currently trying to fit in? Maybe throw in a Beast teacher for good measure? Sounds like a fun premise for a game.<br /> <br /> After all, it's about what you make of it.<br /> I can see why you'd be hesitant about an anime-style school of monster kids, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>exactly, we had a whole thread about high school in the CofD and Hogwarts for tiny magi is awesome too. I wonder what Uratha academy is like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-25-2017, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T15:50:14-07:00","id":1133972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1133951#post1133951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> exactly, we had a whole thread about high school in the CofD and Hogwarts for tiny magi is awesome too. I wonder what Uratha academy is like?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Class, this lesson is true&quot;.<br /> -Spirit Ecology 201 Instructor, Dr. Gurmeet Mishra, Drives-Wisdom-Into-Stone","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T23:39:02-07:00","id":1134068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1133937#post1133937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well shit... Here I was looking for people who've attempted to update Innocents into 2nd friendly for a game I'll be running in about a months time, I find this little gem telling me that the devs are doing just that!!! what!!!??<br /> <br /> So excitement aside, What do I do until it comes out? I was planning on doing an Innocents Char Gen session this very weekend and I haven't the slightest clue on how to do that now. Any ideas? I want 2nd edition rules but also it be an innocents game with innocents chars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most fans agree that best 2E update of Innocents rules is just make 'being child' as Condition ( or series of Conditions ), each generating extra Beats for the child characters. I earlier in this topic thrown proposed by me and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/982910-2e-innocents-children-in-cod\">linked to previous attempts at 2E fan update</a>. Just let me look for it... Oh, here it is!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/982910-2e-innocents-children-in-cod?p=1005718#post1005718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Returning to topic with my straight forward compilation of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> ideas. I added only Attributes cap on <i>Child</i> Condition, but still think that maybe using general -1 penalty to all actions based on Attributes past 3, maybe?<br /> <br /> General idea is that young child ( 7-12ish ) would begin with <i>Child</i>, while a young adult (17-20ish) would start with <i>Adolescent</i>. A Teenager (13-16ish) would get the worst of both worlds and start with both Conditions.<br /> <br /> <b>Child (Persistent)</b><br /> Your character is a pre-adolescent (typically between 7-12 years of age). Character at this stage of development have several disadvantages when compared to an adult; their base size is 4, their Speed factor is 4, and any unarmed attack made against an adult or adult sized creature suffers a -2 penalty. You cannot raise any of her Attributes and Skills above 3 dots. Additionally, you do not benefit from the 10-again quality on teamwork actions that involve adult characters, and adult characters gain the 8-again quality on Contested actions against her. However, the characters smaller stature works to their advantage in some situations; against adults they gain a +1 die bonus to Stealth, Breaking Free of Grapple, or when Dodging.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> When your character reaches physical maturity.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> When the characters youth causes a significant social or physical set back (especially when dealing with adults).<br /> <br /> <b>Adolescent (Persistent)</b><br /> Your character is in an awkward transitionary phase of development - no longer a child, but not yet an adult, she struggles to find her place in the world. Adults tend to assume the worst in your character until she proves her maturity to them. You begin all Social Maneuvering attempts with adult characters at a Hostile impression.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> You face prejudice or discrimination as a result of your age.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Your character reaches developmental maturity.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T23:43:38-07:00","id":1134070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131071-innocents-2e-is-on-its-way?p=1133951#post1133951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what Uratha academy is like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem with Uratha is that they're not always werewolves, sometimes it happens late in life.<br /> <br /> Wolf-blooded are another matter, however, and come with their own problems. I think I had a bunch of scattered ideas written down, I remember I thought it would be an idea that comes up every once and awhile, like the totem behind it kept bringing it to werewolves who needed the cause, the end result being sort of like Xavier's School for Gifted Youngsters. The principal/headmaster would be a werewolf, of course, as would some of the higher faculty and 'recruiters,' who were either graduates who didn't want to leave, or werewolves who liked what the school had to offer and wanted to be a part of it. The faculty would be divided up into different packs and the school itself formed a small protectorate, bound by the lodge that is the academy. They would have to rely a lot on word of mouth as there's only so many orphans to pick up but a lot of werewolf parents who can't deal with being parents, though that could also be dangerous, since a school full of impressionable wolf-blooded would be a nice target for groups like the Fire-Touched or Predator Kings, even some Forsaken and Ghost Wolf groups. I think they had a rival Ivory Claw Academy, as well, sort of like the Brotherhood of Evil Mutant's 'clique' in the X-men high school cartoon.<br /> <br /> Kids would be taught about the spirit but only those with spirit-leaning gifts would really be funneled into proper spirit education, mostly warnings about the dangers of the place, you wouldn't want the kids to get too close a look and see how predatory the whole thing is and balk. Those who transformed early would be shifted into a separate school on the same campus and directed into a pack to get used to the structure. The big point would be getting them ready for the working world while also preparing them for the supernatural and how it may impact them. They'd all take part, knowingly and un, in rites and little things that would help protect and strengthen the school, often disguised as traditions and ceremonies.<br /> <br /> It's basically an inversion of the Talbot House, which thinks lycanthropy is a kind of demonic possession and gathers troubled wolf-blooded kids from their parents, or the law when they're orphans, and tries to get them to 'pray the wolf away.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-26-2017, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}